	<p><strong>A Just and True Return (JTR)</strong> is a database of Pennsylvania’s surviving county slave registries. These documents, collected from more than a dozen repositories in three states, are evidence of gradual abolition’s routinization, of American familial relationships, and of the historical value of studying slavery wherever it existed.</p>

